   Singapore, SINGAPORE, OCT, 2011},
Organization = {Singapore Inst Elect (SIE)},
Abstract = {Recently river corridors in Guangzhou are being focused on as important
   natural networks in urban environment as well as cultural and
   recreational resources. This paper took East Ho Chung River Greenway in
   Guangzhou as an object to do some comprehensive evaluation of its built
   environment by the method of the post occupancy evaluation (POE), such
   as questionnaires, interviews and statistics. The questionnaire is
   divided into 6 categories, such as facilities, green space, signs and
   maps, transport, security and management, and recreational activities in
   external environment. Through the analysis, we identified six human
   dimensions in the studies: cleanliness, aesthetic, comfort, safety,
   suitability and hydrophilic property. As a result of this research, some
   problems on the evaluation were grasped by the hierarchy process
   analysis based on the six categories and user's six human dimensions. We
   concluded by discussing solutions of these problems, and suggested some
   proposals in design to meet the users' requirement for the future
   construction of greenway. This study aims to improve the quality of East
   Ho Chung River Greenway's built environment, and to make the greenway
   design more scientific. (C) 2011 Published by Elsevier Ltd. Selection
   and/or peer-review under responsibility of the Organizers of 2011
   International Conference on Energy and Environmental Science.},
