Abstract = {This study focuses on the role of conceptualisation in capturing the
   urban issues within the studio tutorial learning environment in
   Universiti Teknologi Malaysia. Essentially, it looks into how the
   conceptualisation process during design facilitates students' problem
   solving ability in dealing with tasks in hand. Evidences of this come
   from students' dynamic cognitive interactions with knowledge and
   experience as transpired through the studio environment. The study
   provides insight into the interactive role of experience as a key factor
   in facilitating design conceptualisation process and the course enables
   students to harness relevant problem-solving skills. (C) 2015 The
