Abstract = {Along with the rapid growth of the computer technology, visualization
   has become a medium for the planners and designers to express their idea
   and generate a better mutual understanding with the affected parties. 3D
   visualization is one of the best system that enable people to view any
   ideas from different angle and perspectives without being worried about
   any distortion that might occur. In the built environment field, 3d
   visualization has been implemented for various aiding purposes within
   many process from planning to designing process. The high accuracy of 3D
   visualization increases the effectiveness of presenting ideas and
   analyzing data for various process. On the other hand, urban environment
   caters a huge amount of users utilizing the city space where people with
   different background races and physical abilities navigate through it in
   one time. This paper will study the theoretical framework and the
   application of 3D visualization as an aiding tools from urban
   environment perspectives.},
