@inproceedings{ WOS:000394555000012,
Author = {Anitei, Mihai and Chraif, Mihaela and Buzea, Elena},
Editor = {Todea, GV},
Title = {THE PERCEPTION OF THE POLLUTION AND ITS EFFECT IN BUCHAREST URBAN CITY},
Booktitle = {APPLIED PSYCHOLOGY, THE PERSON AND THE TECHNOLOGIES OF THE XXI CENTURY},
Series = {Conferinta Internationala de Psihologie Aplicata},
Year = {2010},
Pages = {83-92},
Note = {6th International Conference on Applied Psychology, the Person and the
   Technologies of the 21st Century, Timisoara, ROMANIA, OCT 08-11, 2009},
Organization = {Uniunea Fundatia Augusta},
Abstract = {Many programs of the European Commission in the context Thematic
   Strategy on Air Pollution were considered targets and measures aimed at
   controlling the pollution of the ozone layer, pollution created by
   vehicles, new vehicle standards (EURO 5, EURO VI). Achieving Community
   air quality objectives requires an integrated approach involving city
   authorities but most important the perception of the psychologists and
   citizens.
   The objectives: to collect the perceptions of the Psychology students
   about the quality of the urban environment and the pollution factors; to
   identify the measures of increasing the quality of the environment and
   the role of the psychologist in the urban environment.
   The method: The participants: a number of 371 undergraduate students
   from Faculty of Psychology, Bucharest University and Titu Maiorescu
   University, age between 19 and 31 years (m=22.6; S. D= 3.46).
   The. procedure and instruments: the participants answered to the
   questions in the questionnaire Survey on the Quality of the Urban
   Environment{''}, after a previous pilot study on 141 undergraduate
   students. The three factors of the questionnaire: the quality of the
   environment; methods of increasing the quality of the environment and
   the role of the environmental psychologist in Romania was applied on 835
   students in the last three years and a longitudinal study on the same
   generation students until this graduation has been made.
   The results: The quality of the urban environment (air, traffic,
   attractiveness and green areas) was generally considered to be
   statistically significantly poor in Bucharest Urban. area versus
   residential urban areas (p<0.05) but as the results of the longitudinal
   study the urban environment as the attractiveness and green areas has
   been statistically significantly changed for the better (p<0.01). Also
   there were statistically significant changes in the air perception and
   traffic perception (p<0.01), this time in a negative way.
   Conclusions Health and quality of life were the most important reasons
   respondents give for achieving a high quality urban environment. The
   respondents underlined that sustainable urban transport plans will help
   reduce air pollution and noise, and encourage cycling and walking. Also
   they indicated to adopt and apply the European legislation about the
   existing Air Quality, new vehicle standards (EURO 5, EURO VI) noise
   pollution in town and citizens attitude toward keeping the city clean.
   Taking in consideration that the most important factor in convincing
   respondents to make changes in behavior was better environmental
   information the conclusion of the study highlighted the importance of
   developing the environmental psychology field in Romania by trainings,
   educational programs and environmental advisory.},
