   Hand in Hand, Krtiny, CZECH REPUBLIC, MAY 02-04, 2018},
Organization = {Czech Soc Landscape Engineers; Mendel Univ Brno, Fac Forestry \& Wood
   Technol, Dept Landscape Management; State Enterprise Lesy Ceske
   Republiky, S Moravian Region; FS Bohemia Ltd},
Abstract = {The nature and landscape conservation is often the subject of
   discussion, especially in the context of regional development. In
   additions to conservationists and representatives of public authorities,
   there is a group of people that does not agree with declaring of
   conservation in territory which could be potentially declared as
   Protected Landscape Areas (PLAs) and its surroundings. This often leads
   to emotional debates full of counter-arguments. The declaration of the
   Soutok PLA could be a proof of the long-standing dispute over the nature
   conservation. The article deals with the analysis of documents,
   interviews and opinions that was found through the qualitative research
   (Hendl, 2012). The results point the fact that the residents living in
   the PLAs, which are already declared, perceive the territorial
   protection positively. The perceptions and attitudes to protected areas
   have been identified as a key factor for its successful management. The
   problem of the counter-arguments is that there was no tradition of
   participating and there was poor knowledge and poor communication
   between the conservationists and stakeholders.},
