   FITNESS AND HEALTH, VOL 1},
Year = {2010},
Pages = {106-110},
Note = {International Symposium on Children and Youth Fitness and Health,
   Nanjing, PEOPLES R CHINA, OCT 28-31, 2010},
Abstract = {In order to study the environmental factors' comprehensive effects on
   Han urban youth growth, the authors take the 18-year-old as an example,
   using factor analysis and stepwise regression analysis to analyze the
   correlations and importance among the growth score, natural environment
   and socio-economic environment factors. The youth whose growth score
   ranking the top 10 are located in the northern region, and the growth
   score in the northern region is much higher than that in the southern
   region. The growth score and most of climate factors are all
   significantly correlated and the correlation coefficients between the
   growth score and geographical latitude, Earth longitude, annual sunshine
   duration, annual maximal temperature variation is positive correlation,
   while with annual average temperature, annual precipitation, mean
   relative humidity is significant negative correlation, among which
   geographical latitude, annual average temperature and average relative
   humidity are relatively important; the 20 years' change between the
   growth score and the climate is not closely related. The growth score
   and GDP per capita, the number of sickbeds per thousand people, medical
   technicians per thousand people is significantly positive correlation,
   while with Engel's coefficient is significantly negative correlation,
   among which the influence of the number of sickbeds per thousand people
   is much higher. Among the natural environment and socio-economic
   environment factors, the average relative humidity, the earth longitude
   and the number of sickbeds per thousand people are relatively important.
   The influence of the natural environment and socio-economic environment
   on Han urban youth growth level is integrated and interactive.},
