   SOCIETY AND TOURISM MANAGEMENT SESSION, PT II},
Year = {2010},
Pages = {121-126},
Note = {6th Euro-Asia Conference on Environment and Corporate Social
   Responsibility, Istanbul, TURKEY, MAR 18-19, 2010},
Organization = {German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; IMRE African Alumni Network},
Abstract = {In this paper, the authors conduct a sophisticated questionnaire survey,
   which is designed to synthesize all related information on resident's
   perception of tourism destination. The initial attempts of this
   questionnaire design incorporating five aspects, i.e. economic impact;
   environmental impact; social and cultural impact; participation in
   tourism management; and an overall perception and attitude. For each
   aspect, the questionnaire includes both positive and negative effect
   questions. A pre-test was carried out through a small group of residents
   to exam soundness of survey forms. SPSS16.0 was used to analyze the
   reliability and validity of the collected data. After removing those
   with low statistically correlated survey questions, a questionnaire was
   modified and used for a formal large sample survey. The statistical test
   results indicated that the questionnaire shows a very high reliability
   and validity. Due to limited space, the paper only gave a detailed
   description for two of the five residents' perception categories
   including environmental impacts, and participation in tourism management
   toward tourism development.},
