   CORPORATE SOCIAL RESPONSIBILITY: TOURISM, SOCIETY AND EDUCATION SESSION,
   PT I},
Year = {2014},
Pages = {84-88},
Note = {10th Euro-Asia Conference on Environment and Corporate Social
   Responsibility - Tourism, Society and Education Session, Berlin,
   GERMANY, AUG 29-30, 2014},
Organization = {Tianjin Univ Finance \& Econ, Tourism Dept; IMRE Alumni Network; German
   Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; TU Bergakademie Freiberg},
Abstract = {In recent years, moral education which contributes to translate moral
   cognization into moral behaviors attracts wide attention in China.
   Researches of the author show that the translation of moral cognization
   into moral behaviors works through two kinds of spirit strength, i.e.
   volition basing on ration and emotion. Confucius's moral education of
   ``Canonizing Qing{''} stresses mainly on emotion. On the one hand, the
   moral cognization possesses strong force resulting from education; on
   the other hand, it facilitates the translation of moral cognization into
   moral behaviors by exserting behavior function of consanguineous
   emotion. Thus, one can say that Confucius's moral education of
   ``Canonizing Qing{''} have important meaning in terms of turning moral
   cognization into moral behaviors.},
