   the 21st Century, RHODES, GREECE, SEP 08-10, 1999},
Organization = {Wessex Inst Technol},
Abstract = {In the city Gaziantep a shopping centre was built at city centre without
   giving consideration to the traffic problem. By looking at the number
   one can see that traffic flow nearly doubled (166\%), even though
   shopping centre added its own parking space which was 300 before and is
   550 now. There is considerable difficulty finding parking in the area.
   By evaluating the numbers in the table we see that some people working
   in the area stop driving to work today. The parking problem has became
   worst especially at shopping hours from 11:00 till 18:00, After 18:00
   due to the business closing, problem is a little alleviated.},
