Abstract = {This research focuses upon the socio-environmental dimensions and urban
   identity of urban environments by evaluating human behaviours and
   space-to-human relations. In addition, approaches to urban re-branding
   will be analysed to evaluate the role of engineered identities in
   enhancing social integration. This particular study will focus upon the
   installation of temporary activities into the public realm and the
   impact that these can have upon perception, identity and activity within
   public spaces. A case study of temporary markets taking place in
   Nottingham's Old Market Square in the UK will be evaluated to explore
