   Tatras, Adm Off},
Abstract = {Despite reduction in emissions continues, many cities and surrounding
   areas struggles with high concentration of harmful air pollution, which
   is currently still very actual and persistent problem. Calculation of
   immission pollution from various sources through the models is an
   important tool for assessing the state of air pollution in the urban and
   non- urban environment. The material conditions of work are models
   designed for the pollution source located in urban area environment, and
   the same pollution source located in the non- urban area. In the harsh
   urban area environment, turbulences are created, which contributes to
   the intensive mixture of polluted air and therefore a lower
   concentration are achieved but the impact of the source of pollution is
   greater. In the non-urban conditions is the surface smooth and
   ``laminar{''} is achieving (particularly characteristic for coastal
   areas) which has higher concentration and the impact is decreasing,
