Note = {Australian Sociological Associations Sociology of Emotions and Affect
   Midyear Symposium, Adelaide, AUSTRALIA, JUL 25-26, 2013},
Abstract = {Emotions are an emergent feature of interaction, and many of the
   articles in this special section touch on this. What I find interesting
   is that we get a glimpse into how emotions unfold in a situation, and
   how the flow of emotions in any study can run from participant to
   participant, participant to researcher, and researcher to participant.
   Part of this flow of emotions is influenced by reflexivity or the
   awareness of self and other feeling states, which is addressed by some
   of the contributors. What is particularly challenging is how to
   carefully study emotions as they surface in situations, and many of the
   contributors encourage us to pause and think about how to do this.},
