   Buildings/3rd International Conference on Built Environment and Public
   Health, Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY 29-31, 2009},
Organization = {Hunan Univ; Univ Hong Kong; Tsinghua Univ},
Abstract = {The aim of this study was to reveal the characteristics of energy
   consumption of urban inhabitant in China, including gas usages, indoor
   air temperature and relative air humidity, during 2007. In this study,
   six urban houses located in Shanghai, Changsha and Harbin were
   investigated. These cities belong to different climate zones in China.
   It was found that heating consumption of these houses, except district
   heating houses, appeared mainly in January with temperature varied from
   10 to 15 degrees C. For the case of Harbin, since heating energy
   consumption in winter was not known, there were no significant changes
   of energy consumption of the houses among winter, summer and other
   seasons. Indoor temperature of Harbin was around 25 degrees C.},
