   (URDC), Famagusta, CYPRUS, DEC 07-09, 2011},
Abstract = {Quality physical environment could contribute towards the creation of a
   healing environment. This paper, an outcome of an ongoing research on
   physical qualities of Malaysian paediatric wards investigated the design
   trend upon users' satisfaction. Two UK NHS evaluation toolkits were used
   to evaluate the quality of the physical environment and the users'
   satisfaction levels. Data collected involved paediatric wards in eight
   hospitals and respondents comprised of 215 nurses and 217 patients.
   Results revealed that the positive design trend was not in tandem with
   the users' satisfactory level. Lack of understanding upon users' needs
   is suspect in designing those wards. (C) 2012 Published by Elsevier B.V.
