   CORPORATE SOCIAL RESPONSIBILITY: MANAGEMENT SCIENCE AND ENGINEERING, PT
   II},
Year = {2009},
Pages = {50-56},
Note = {5th Euro-Asia Conference on Environment and Corporate Social
   Responsibility - Management Science and Engineering, Kumasi, GHANA, JUL
   03-04, 2009},
Abstract = {``The Grand Canal{''} has been regarded as the longest man-made river
   and greatest irrigation project. It plays an indispensable role in
   economic and cultural development, and communication between north and
   south of China. The cultural significance and characteristics of the
   Grand Canal can be nominated as a World Heritage property However, many
   adverse consequences have been brought about as a result of rapid
   economic growth in recent years, which become obstacles to the
   sustainable development of the region. With respect to the concept of
   cultural routes and the current urban environmental status of the
   region, the authors provide several suggestions on urban environmental
   protection and management strategies, which facilitate the sustainable
   development of the region.},
