Note = {21st Scientific Conference on Energy and the Environment, Opatija,
   CROATIA, OCT 22-24, 2008},
Abstract = {A few years ago, the French Academy of Technology (FAT) organized a
   workshop on Energy in the 21(st) century. A group of specialists, after
   an analysis of the evolution of the energy issue from the beginning of
   the industrial era, and discussion on the subject during several days,
   came up with two scenarios concerning energy and energy use in the
   21(st) century. The scenarios are based on a specific methodology which
   the FAT group proposed.
   These very interesting scenarios spur reflection on the road transport
   problem as the most dependent on fossil fuels, having heavy impact on
   the environment and global warming, and being of paramount importance
   for the economy. This paper gives an overview of the two scenarios in
   order to achieve an the energy,frame of reference for the urban
   transport situation, as the sector which has a huge impact on the
   economic activity, energy in general, environment and social life.
   An overview of the Study of alternative technologies and fuels for urban
   transport buses, made by Brodarski Institut for the Transport department
   of Zagreb authority, is given in the paper as an analytical part of the
   transportation problem. On the other side, urban transportation is
   considered in light of the energy problem in general, as the qualitative
   part of the analysis. The article points out that urban transport has a
   special role in the process of decreasing fossil fuel dependence, and
   the necessity for rapid alternative technology implementation, as well
   as development of the urban transport system itself.},
