Abstract = {While Malaysia is heading for urbanization, urban green space
   degradation had occurred. Malaysia's typical urban green space had shown
   the demotion of social interaction among urban residents. Hence, this
   research aimed to understand the designs of typical Malaysian green
   spaces which are believed to enhance community social interactions.
   Variables measured werethe physical and natural characters of selected
   green spaces including activities, attractions and settings. The
   observation took place during representative of weekday, weekend and
   public holiday in those green spaces. The result suggested that
   diversity of subspaces including vegetation density, animal populations,
   undulating landforms and water bodies afford social interaction
