Year = {2021},
Volume = {38},
Month = {JUL},
Note = {10th International Conference on Urban Climate (ICUC), New York, NY, AUG
   06-10, 2018},
Abstract = {The Urban Climate and Resiliency-Science Working Group (i.e., The WG)
   was convened in the summer of 2018 to explore the scientific grand
   challenges related to climate resiliency of cities. The WG leveraged the
   presentations at the 10th International Conference on Urban Climate
   (ICUC10) held in New York City (NYC) on 6-10 August 2018 as input forum.
   ICUC10 was a collaboration between the International Association of
   Urban Climate, American Meteorological Society, and World Meteorological
   Organization. It attracted more than 600 participants from more than 50
   countries, resulting in close to 700 oral and poster presentations under
   the common theme of ``Sustainable \& Resilient Urban Environments{''}.
   ICUC10 covered topics related to urban climate and weather processes
   with far-reaching implications to weather forecasting, climate change
   adaptation, air quality, health, energy, urban planning, and governance.
   This article provides a synthesis of the analysis of the current state
   of the art and of the recommendations of the WG for future research
   along each of the four Grand Challenges in the context of urban climate
   and weather resiliency; Modeling, Observations, Cyber-Informatics, and
   Knowledge Transfer \& Applications.},
